troduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:2c37c3c20a9e85a18ec0ed0fb6816e690ecb324451f1d1631fa6dfaf4774363b","file":"preprints/Topological-triviality-of-mu-constant-families-of-surface-singularities-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":32,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"24f3b66b32b00e8c2213966c750e6f94383ce9f2b212ee508dc809db0b9afed7","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Topological-triviality-of-mu-constant-families-of-surface-singularities-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:2c37c3c20a9e85a18ec0ed0fb6816e690ecb324451f1d1631fa6dfaf4774363b","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Topological-triviality-of-mu-constant-families-of-surface-singularities-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L32"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $F:(\\mathbb C^3\\times\\Delta,\\{0\\}\\times\\Delta)\\to(\\mathbb C,0)$\nbe holomorphic.  Suppose that, for every $t\\in\\Delta$, $f_t(0)=0$,\n$f_t$ has an isolated critical point at $0$, and\n$\\mu(f_t,0)=\\mu(f_0,0)$.  After shrinking the disk and the germ\nrepresentatives, there is a homeomorphism germ\n\\[\n \\Phi(x,t)=(\\phi_t(x),t),\\qquad\n \\phi_t(0)=0,\\quad \\phi_0=\\mathrm{id},\\qquad\n f_t\\bigl(\\phi_t(x)\\bigr)=f_0(x).\n\\]\nBoth $\\Phi$ and $\\Phi^{-1}$ are jointly continuous on neighborhoods\nof the origin section over the original disk."}
